}

^["risk_model"]{
 # hard_failures: any of 344 corpus files failing parse after PARTICLE changes
 # soft_failures: emit/skim/corpus counters that regex for #> needing re-pointing
 # non_negotiables: corpus stays PARSEABLE (the operational floor)
 # relaxed 2026-07-23 (user): byte-stability/shape preservation is NOT sacred — "not very attached to existing .spw documents"; deliberate surface refactors are welcome when they improve interpretability. Wonder about syntax freely; refactor corpus later.
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-07-23 03:05] observe — #: and #> fall to Prose; #!/## lex clean; ~# has its own matchAnnotation. Inconsistent recognition of one family: ⟨stance⟩#⟨aim⟩name.
 >>[2026-07-23 03:06] decide — treat as one DIRECTIVE token family with stance (prefix) and aim (postfix) slots; # is the resonance/metadata plane, stance = modality entering the plane (~ defer, $ substrate, = config…), aim = what the mark does (> points, : classifies, ! asserts).
 >>[2026-07-23 03:08] observe — wild exotics ($#e, =#p) prove authors already compose stances; lattice recognition legitimizes existing practice rather than inventing new syntax.
 >>[2026-07-23 03:10] decide — user aims recorded: (1) enhanced indexing + discoverable referential patterns + new structured-relationship encodings; (2) Spw ethos — expressive cognitive modeling, constructs that invite wonder; (3) renaming the combinatorics is open. Renames = concept vocabulary, never sigils.
 >>[2026-07-23 03:12] decide — anchored-node relation: a directive binds to the expression that FOLLOWS it (doc-comment placement). #>anchor → the next node is the anchored node; that binding is the export/index table fragments resolve into.
 >>[2026-07-23 03:20] decide — naming = LINGUISTIC PARTICLES (user): family `particle ⟨stance⟩#⟨aim⟩name`; #> deixis (points at the node that follows), #: case (classifies bearer's role), #! mood (asserts pragmatic force), ~# aspect (deferred state-in-time). Sigils unchanged; code/types/canon adopt the vocabulary.
 >>[2026-07-23 03:40] note — detour before commit 2 (user): evaluated the grok stash for integration. Verdict: main's reconciliation already superseded it — all three insertion-heavy residues (topography-scan local types, vscode roots.ts hardcoded map, dev.ts inlined walker) move logic OUT of shared modules, opposite of the new module-consumability priority. Payload archived on feature/grok-lsp-reconciliation.
 >>[2026-07-23 03:55] implement — commit 2: matchParticle lexes #>name (deixis) and #:name (case) as single PARTICLE tokens (aim in token.kind), registered before the operator matcher. Deliberately incremental: #!/##/~#/#[ untouched; bare #>/#: without a name left alone; strings safe. Corpus: 344/344 parse, token count 190858→187538 (~3.3k particles unified). Gates: types baseline, seed 370+6, cli 101; runtime failures (4) confirmed pre-existing via clean-branch stash check.
 >>[2026-07-23 04:15] implement — commit 3 (grammar + binding): ParticleNode term (aim/name/span, TermNode union) parsed via particleNode beside annotationNode; PARTICLE added to isSpwTrigger so particles break prose accumulation (the real fix — canon files open with # prose comments, headers lived in ProseChunk TEXT). particleBindings/deixisTable exported: runs of marks (particle-led or boundary-less ops) flow to the first content item; scans Sequences AND Prose chunks. Verified on real canon: bias-product 3 anchors, orphaned-files 2 (matches user screenshot breadcrumb), index 3, all bound. Gates: 344/344, types 4 baseline, seed 376+5, cli 101, runtime pre-existing.
 >>[2026-07-23 04:16] note — user screenshot: vscode extension already renders Local/Ambient Braids from these marks — the UI consumer deixisTable is built for. Interop path: braids-from-seed-API replaces braids-from-regex.
 >>[2026-07-23 04:17] note — isMarkLike (boundary-less op) doubles as the first noise detector for the census: it is exactly the "underspecified operator use" class the user flagged for lint/mutation rules.
 >>[2026-07-23 05:10] decide — design direction (user: cache tier × directives, consequence familiarity, language physics): STANCE = CACHE POLICY. ~# aspect = mutable/expiring tier (wip cache blocks are aspect marks), bare particles = durable canon, $# = substrate-computed, =# = pinned. Extension: deixis tables cacheable per file-hash; aspect always re-read; workspaceTemperature weighted by aspect density. Census produces AIM-MIX DIALECT PROFILES (deixis=navigability, case=queryability, mood=assertion richness, aspect=volatility) reflected back in the extension — familiarity via feedback, not docs. particle-physics section joins brace-physics at commit 10.
 >>[2026-07-23 05:11] decide — user: LSP/extension enhancements along the way. Insert spw/particles custom request (deixis table + aim mix per document) after CLI consumers, before coverage.
 >>[2026-07-23 05:45] implement — commits 6-9 landed: fragment keystone (resolveFragment + BiasTarget.fragment), CLI consumers (mount verifies anchors w/ suggestions — canon's 3 deep-links verify through; expand projects anchored regions), spw/particles LSP request (deixis table + aim mix), particle census (spw:census). Census findings: corpus mix 600/1058/1011/2201 (deixis/case/mood/aspect); docs = aspect-heavy volatile tier (1147); 7 duplicate anchors all explainable (init templates, lib version copies); 0 unbound anchors; 1527 noise marks dominated by #-comment continuations → lint rule needs comment filtering.
 >>[2026-07-23 05:46] note — parallel session installed VS Code + Neovim plugins against the shared LSP; Memory Hot/Warm/Cold panel exists with zero data — the stance-tier consumer for aspect-density warmth. spw/particles reaches editors on next LSP restart. Remaining: commit 10 (canon registry w/ glossary lead: particle=family, anchor=deixis's bookmark) + comment-filtered noise lint + aspect migration.
 >>[2026-07-23 03:22] decide — user: recognize FILE PATTERNS for semantic depth. First-class pattern: the header particle stack (deixis + case/mood pair — `#>anchor` `#:layer #!pragmatics`) opening ~every canonical file. Census commit added: discover recurring particle stacks corpus-wide (spw:formula/analyze), name them in the registry, refactor only where a recognized pattern adds nuance — never mechanical rewriting.
}

